      "observed": "U2 ~CS (pin 6) is on NET0010 with U10 GPIO7 (pin 21); U5 ~CS (pin 6) is on NET0016 with U10 GPIO4 (pin 18); U9 ~CS (pin 6) is on NET0012 with U10 GPIO6 (pin 20).",
      "expected": "Per the specification, the three MAX31855 chip selects should be driven by ESP32 GPIO4, GPIO6, and GPIO7 respectively (U2 on GPIO4, U3 on GPIO6, U4 on GPIO7). In this build the first thermocouple channel (U2) is instead on GPIO7, the second (U5) on GPIO4, and the third (U9) on GPIO6.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Each chip has its own independent chip-select: ~{CS} (pin 6) on U2/U3/U4 goes to separate nets CS0/CS1/CS2, driven by ESP32 GPIO4/GPIO6/GPIO7 respectively."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"10\") (name \"NET0010\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"21\") (pinfunction \"GPIO7\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"~{CS}\") (pintype \"input\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"14\") (name \"NET0016\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"18\") (pinfunction \"GPIO4/ADC1_CH4\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"~{CS}\") (pintype \"input\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"11\") (name \"NET0012\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"20\") (pinfunction \"GPIO6\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"~{CS}\") (pintype \"input\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The firmware will select the wrong MAX31855 channel for each thermocouple zone, causing temperature readings to be associated with the wrong physical connector. This could lead to incorrect oven temperature control and potential overheating if the wrong zone is used for feedback.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a thermocouple chip-select mapping anomaly: the three MAX31855 ~CS lines are connected to ESP32 GPIO pins in a different order than specified, which would cause the firmware to read the wrong thermocouple zone."
}

